Wiki Page tables: "Footer row" in the cell toolbar adds a footer row at the bottom of the table (and removes it again); a footer cell can show the sum of its column ("Sum" in the cell toolbar), updated while editing and stored with the page. The footer row is neither sorted nor filtered in the view. The demo page "Projektbudget 2026" ships its "Gesamt" row as footer with sums. @reekitconcept
